  "deneshkar_explanation": {
    "file": "members/member4-IT24103828/Understanding_Submitted_20261008.md",
    "sha256": "3c95c9a3eb7b13e0b35278526e053beedb70aab4920297d9c3db90a32f02c879",
    "text": "The 10:00\u201311:00 shift passes because the existing shift finishes exactly at 10:00. The new shift starts at 10:00, so the two shifts only touch at the boundary; their working times do not overlap. Therefore, the agent returns APPROVE.\nWhen I change the new shift's start time to 09:30, it overlaps the existing 09:00\u201310:00 shift for 30 minutes, from 09:30 to 10:00. The agent detects this as double booking. Because the problem can be fixed by changing the shift time, it returns REVISE instead of APPROVE."
